---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Civic Pulse"
  description="Learn about Civic Pulse, its official sources, and how to reuse Civic Pulse content under CC BY 4.0."
>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="page-intro">
      <h1>About Civic Pulse</h1>
      <p>Civic Pulse is civic infrastructure for the people who show up.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>A clearer signal from city hall</h2>
      <p>
        Local decisions shape daily life, but they rarely reach the people they
        affect. Civic Pulse turns agendas, votes, and public comment into
        something you can follow — and act on.
      </p>

      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/maps/">Explore maps</a> to see the places, precincts, and
        layers that make up a community. Visit the{' '}
        <a href="/calendar/">community calendar</a> to find public meetings,
        gatherings, and deadlines. Browse <a href="/people/">people</a>,{' '}
        <a href="/orgs/">organizations</a>, <a href="/elections/">elections</a>,{' '}
        and <a href="/legislation/">legislation</a> to follow the people and
        decisions that shape your community. No account is required to browse
        public information.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sources">Official sources and credits</h2>
      <p>
        Civic Pulse credits the public agencies and staff who publish the
        original records that make civic research possible. These official
        sources provide local government, election, and legislative information:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.maconbibb.us/">Macon-Bibb County Government</a>{' '}
          — county departments, commissioners, public notices, and meeting information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.maconbibb.us/board-of-elections/">Macon-Bibb County Board of Elections</a>{' '}
          — local election notices, ballots, and voting information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://sos.ga.gov/">Georgia Secretary of State</a>{' '}
          — statewide election information and official business records.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.legis.ga.gov/">Georgia General Assembly</a>{' '}
          — state legislators, bills, and legislative proceedings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.congress.gov/">Congress.gov, Library of Congress</a>{' '}
          — federal legislation, members, and congressional records.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Follow the source links on individual records for the specific documents,
        recordings, and publishers behind them. This list is a starting point;
        individual records may credit additional agencies and publishers.
        Civic Pulse summaries and transcripts may contain errors or omit context.
        Check the original source for the latest details and the full record.
      </p>

      <h2 id="license">Share and reuse: CC BY 4.0</h2>
      <p>
        Except where otherwise noted, original content created by Civic Pulse is
        shared under the{' '}
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) license</a>.
        You may copy, redistribute, and adapt this content, including for
        commercial purposes, under the license terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        When reusing content, credit Civic Pulse and any named contributors,
        link to the original page and the license, and indicate any changes.
        Retain supplied attribution notices and do not imply endorsement.
        Do not impose additional legal or technological restrictions on the
        freedoms the license grants.
      </p>
      <p>
        Example credit: “Source: Civic Pulse, [original page title and URL],
        licensed under CC BY 4.0. Changes: [describe your changes, if any].”
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party documents, photographs, logos, recordings, maps, and linked
        articles remain subject to their own rights and license terms; they are
        not automatically covered by Civic Pulse’s license. Material already in
        the public domain remains in the public domain.
      </p>

      <h2>Communities first</h2>
      <p>
        Civic Pulse is not affiliated with any county, city, or organization
        listed on this site. Always confirm details with the original publisher.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
